[
    {
        "text": "The logic behind why a DAO works is about making assumptions about incentives. Users who own tokens in a project have voting power. The more tokens you own, the more voting power you have. Therefore, users are incentivized to act in good faith to keep the project healthy and robust. They will harm themselves if they do bad things because their token's value will be jeopardized. There are many benefits of a DAO without a central authority. A DAO distributes the decision making power to a group of mostly anonymous users who have skin in the game. It makes the decision making process aligned, as the decision makers are the ones who will be impacted directly by their decisions. Token holders also feel a sense of ownership and empowerment when they have a direct say in decision making.",
        "start": 800,
        "end": 46700,
        "confidence": 0.9808515,
        "channel": null,
        "speaker": "A",
